# CLAUDE.md - local development instructions
CLAUDE.md

# Rust build artifacts
/target/

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This crate is not a plain library: the
# gemspec ships the lockfile INSIDE the gem and extconf.rb compiles the extension
# on the installing machine, so the lock is a build input of the published
# artifact rather than a local convenience. Untracked, a fresh clone has no lock,
# `gem build` silently omits it (Dir[] just fails to match), and every install
# re-resolves dependencies at compile time -- so two installs of the same gem
# version can be built against different crates. The gemspec now refuses to build
# without it; this line is what keeps it present.

